      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1751990088887,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "consistent hashing",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "consistent hashing",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jtw2H-eRgaCHbdM5ZgRYM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13137.754285828392,
      "y": 1718.3654858984794,
      "width": 618.699462890625,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bDS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2016032647,
      "version": 1604,
      "versionNonce": 2016051766,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1751995253670,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scaling:\n\n- chat server -> with sticky load balancer and service deiscover\n- pubusb -> consistent hashing.\n- messageing server -> stateless.\n- chat db ->  300k / s -> 1B/ day\n-> 30 days -> 30B -> 1 row -> 200B -> 6 * 10^12 -> 3TB \n\nwhat if we are saving message in db -> \nbiggest problem is message db that can be shift to \nor partition with help of date. \nold can be shift to other place. \n\nand in general \nall db would be like dynamodb\nand partition by userId\n\npartition key -> userId -> in usertable\nin chatmember also, in chat its chatId. \nget chat from chatmember. \nin message its userId\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Scaling:\n\n- chat server -> with sticky load balancer and service deiscover\n- pubusb -> consistent hashing.\n- messageing server -> stateless.\n- chat db ->  300k / s -> 1B/ day\n-> 30 days -> 30B -> 1 row -> 200B -> 6 * 10^12 -> 3TB \n\nwhat if we are saving message in db -> \nbiggest problem is message db that can be shift to \nor partition with help of date. \nold can be shift to other place. \n\nand in general \nall db would be like dynamodb\nand partition by userId\n\npartition key -> userId -> in usertable\nin chatmember also, in chat its chatId. \nget chat from chatmember. \nin message its userId\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
