      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1751989217790,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "get all chats.\nget messages for a chat\ncreate chat etc.",
      "fontSize": 16.09652686371245,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "get all chats.\nget messages for a chat\ncreate chat etc.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Gl7dkY36GBjYBd0M71dV6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13364.324612046927,
      "y": 1222.3280609181397,
      "width": 1000.5794677734375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bDX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 427882505,
      "version": 1655,
      "versionNonce": 10597098,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1751991263353,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Edge cases:\n - normal api failure like list of chats, list of message -> retry by client. \n - chat server crash.\n    - user send message , but chat server crash\n         - retry popup and resend paginated request and chat connection.\n    - user send save in db but crash\n         -  again retry so it will fetch from db latest one messages. \n    - user 2 offline -> can check in session, or even if we send in pubsub, \n      there won't be consumer to listen and its like fire and forget\n    - db latency ? \n        - we can decouple but will have to deal with eventual consistency in worst case.\n    - what if pubsub crashes\n        - let say sender sent \"a\" first, receiver will receive, then send \"b\", but before that pubsub crash.\n        - before sending -> sender send to other redis and similar consumer receive\n        - just after ? -> bit tough it will connect to new pubusb and start receiving new message.\n        - for handling these cases, in message we can maintain the previous message\n          so at client side it will see ordering and refetch explicitly\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Edge cases:\n - normal api failure like list of chats, list of message -> retry by client. \n - chat server crash.\n    - user send message , but chat server crash\n         - retry popup and resend paginated request and chat connection.\n    - user send save in db but crash\n         -  again retry so it will fetch from db latest one messages. \n    - user 2 offline -> can check in session, or even if we send in pubsub, \n      there won't be consumer to listen and its like fire and forget\n    - db latency ? \n        - we can decouple but will have to deal with eventual consistency in worst case.\n    - what if pubsub crashes\n        - let say sender sent \"a\" first, receiver will receive, then send \"b\", but before that pubsub crash.\n        - before sending -> sender send to other redis and similar consumer receive\n        - just after ? -> bit tough it will connect to new pubusb and start receiving new message.\n        - for handling these cases, in message we can maintain the previous message\n          so at client side it will see ordering and refetch explicitly\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
